# PLAN3-RT — TimeCap on CLI main

File: openOODA/audit/plan3_rt.oot
Wave 0 RT proof. Seed compiler only. No product edit. No oodac patch. No chs_rt patch.

Logline: The seed compiler typechecks and lowers a CLI main that takes FsCap, SysCap, and TimeCap.
Setup: Worktree `/home/jeryd/.grok/worktrees/ooda-bench`. Seed `bootstrap/seed/oodac`. Scratch proofs live only under `/tmp/grok-goal-e3250e659225/implementer`.
Beats:
  1. Read the product CLI main and the C emit grant path.
  2. Check existing TimeCap fixtures with the seed.
  3. Check and emit-c a tiny three-cap main in scratch.

## 0. Verdict

TimeCap on main: YES

The seed compiler accepts `pub fn main(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap, args: List[String])`.
It lowers that main to C. It injects `oo_cap_grant_time()`. It lowers `now_ms(time)` to `oo_now_ms(time)`.
Ship 3 is not blocked. Do not fall back to `date`.

A capability is a typed token that grants one sealed effect.

