```
SEED=./bootstrap/seed/oodac
SCRATCH=/tmp/grok-goal-e3250e659225/implementer
$SEED check  $SCRATCH/timecap_main_cli_shape.oo
$SEED emit-c $SCRATCH/timecap_main_cli_shape.oo
```

Recorded result (2026-08-17):

  - `check` prints `OK` and exits 0.
  - `emit-c` exits 0. Stderr is empty.
  - Seed sha256: `077d0f883edb083bc2598c0f1f87469d7a091c53e3db1ffd826f2cf5b046fef2`

Scratch source used for that command:

```
pub fn main(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap, args: List[String]) {
    let t0: Int = now_ms(time);
    println(t0);
}
```

C emit of that main (trimmed):

```
int main(int argc, char **argv) {
  long long fs = oo_cap_grant_fs();
  long long sys = oo_cap_grant_sys();
  long long time = oo_cap_grant_time();
  /* other ambient grants */
  fs = oo_cap_grant_fs();
  sys = oo_cap_grant_sys();
  time = oo_cap_grant_time();
  OoSList args = oo_slist_new();
  long long t0 = oo_now_ms(time);
}
```

The same seed also accepts:

  - `main(time: &TimeCap)` with `now_ms(time)`
  - `main(fs: &FsCap, sys: &SysCap, time: &TimeCap)` with `now_ms(time)`
  - `main(..., time_cap: &TimeCap, args: List[String])` with `now_ms(time_cap)`

  Last case emits `long long time_cap = oo_cap_grant_time();` then `oo_now_ms(time_cap)`.

