This note does not add TimeCap. DE2 owns that edit.

## 3. How the seed injects main caps

C emit is the product lower path (`bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` uses emit-c + gcc).

`oodac/c_emit_fn.oo` always injects ambient grants into `int main(int argc, char **argv)`:

  - `long long fs = oo_cap_grant_fs();`
  - `long long sys = oo_cap_grant_sys();`
  - `long long time = oo_cap_grant_time();`

`oodac/c_emit_skip_grant.oo` maps type `TimeCap` to grant suffix `time`.
For each main parameter of a known cap type it then rebinds the C name:
`time = oo_cap_grant_time();`

`oodac/c_emit_lower.oo` lowers `now_ms` only when the first argument is a cap identifier.
The C call is `oo_now_ms(name)`.
A literal first argument fails closed:
`ERR c_emit now_ms requires &TimeCap as first arg (not int/lit)`

Runtime already implements the grant and the clock in `runtime/chs_rt_time_rand.c`:
`oo_cap_grant_time` and `oo_now_ms` (requires a live TimeCap token).

DE2 may name the parameter `time` or `time_cap`. Both lower on emit-c.

## 4. Fixtures that already use now_ms

Seed `check` of these files is `OK` exit 0:

  - `bootstrap/corpus/check/pass/ok_now_ms.oo`
    Helper `tick(t: &TimeCap)` calls `now_ms(t)`. `main()` has no TimeCap.
  - `bootstrap/corpus/check/pass/ok_sleep_ms.oo`
    `pub fn main(time: &TimeCap)` calls `sleep_ms(time, 1)`.
  - `fixtures/chrono_smoke_proof.oo`
    `pub fn main(time_cap: &TimeCap)` calls `chrono_now_ms(time_cap)`.
  - `std/time/chrono.oo`
    `chrono_now_ms` forwards to `now_ms(time_cap)`.

Negative fixture `bootstrap/corpus/check/fail/no_cap_now_ms.oo` calls `now_ms()` with no TimeCap.

`emit-c` of `ok_sleep_ms.oo` exits 1 with:
`ERRc_emitunknown free call needs annotationoo_sleep_ms`
That error is a let-bind of `sleep_ms`, not a TimeCap-on-main reject.
The TimeCap grant still appears: `time = oo_cap_grant_time();`
Do not treat that file as a TimeCap blocker.

## 5. LLVM residual (not the product path)

`seed emit-llvm` of the three-cap main exits 0.
`oodac/llvm_emit_fn.oo` grants only `fs`, `sys`, `env`, and `net` by parameter name.
It stores `0` into `%time.slot`. It calls `@now_ms`, not `@oo_now_ms`.

Product rebuild is C emit. INT must use seed `oodac_pure_build`, not `--backend llvm`.
This LLVM gap is not a ship-3 blocker. Do not patch oodac.

